jobs.description:
Are you an enthusiastic Order Picker with EPT experience, or are you eager to learn? We are looking for motivated candidates to join a modern logistics company in Helmond. As an Order Picker with EPT, you will be responsible for collecting, checking, and moving goods throughout the warehouse. Your work ensures that customer orders are processed accurately and shipped on time.

Your responsibilities:

- Picking customer orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking orders before shipment;
- Moving goods and pallets using an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Wrapping, labeling, and scanning pallets;
- Performing Value Added Services (VAS) activities;
- Supporting various warehouse and logistics processes;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized working environment.

Working Hours in the regular day shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule applies:

- 06:00 AM – 03:00 PM
- 03:00 PM – 12:00 AM

- Has experience operating an EPT or is willing to learn;
- Fulltime available;
- Is flexible regarding tasks and working hours;
- Performs well under pressure;
- Enjoys working in a team;
- Has a good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Has a proactive and hands-on attitude.

The Re-Use department is different from a typical warehouse operation. Instead of handling standard products, you work with high-value technical components used by ASML.

Your job is to make sure these parts are received, checked, processed and prepared for their next step. Because of the variety of tasks, every day brings something different.

Your responsibilities may include:

- Receiving and checking incoming materials;
- Scanning and processing products in the system;
- Inspecting parts for quality and completeness;
- Sorting and storing materials;
- Picking orders;
- Packing and preparing shipments;
- Processing logistics data accurately.

Whether you already have warehouse experience or are looking for a new opportunity, there are several areas within the department where you can develop your skills.

- Good communication skills in English;
- Full-time availability;
- A positive and motivated attitude;
- Accuracy and attention to detail;
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

SamenvattingStep into the world of logistics as an Orderpicker at Albert Heijn. This is your chance to join a dynamic team, develop your skills, and enjoy real growth opportunities in a modern warehouse environment. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker at Albert Heijn Bleiswijk, you play a vital role in keeping the online orders running smoothly. Your daily routine includes picking orders with a handheld scanner, checking the quality of products, and managing stock levels. With the scanner, you’ll see exactly which item goes to which location, scan barcodes, and ensure every order is accurate. You’ll work in a modern warehouse, often in cool conditions to keep products fresh. The environment is lively, with team members supporting each other to get the job done. 
Your main tasks are:
- Picking online orders using a scanner;
- Checking order quality before shipment;
- Managing and organizing stock in the warehouse;
- Following clear location and barcode systems;
- Collaborating with your team to meet daily targets.

You’ll work in a 3-shift system: 
- Morningshift: 06:00 – 14:30;
- Afternoonshift: 14:30 – 23:00; 
- Nightshift: 23:00 – 06:00.

Over het bedrijfYou will be working at the Albert Heijn warehouse in Bleiswijk, where groceries are collected and prepared for shipment on a daily basis. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that orders are processed accurately and on time. You will join a diverse team where colleagues help one another and work together to achieve daily goals. Naturally, you won't be on your own as a new team member; you will receive guidance from a buddy to help you quickly learn the ropes and find your place within the team.
Wat wij vragen- Own accommodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- At least 1 year of experience as an Orderpicker or in a similar logistical job;
- Able to communicate in English at a basic level;
- Willing to work in a 3-shift system and on weekends;
- Working in a cold enviro

In the department where you will be working (High Care), we make delicious lunch and meal salads. As Operator (we also call it line manager), you are responsible for setting up and operating the machine and you keep the total overview of the production line. You are the first point of contact for 6 to 12 production employees working on the line.

Your tasks:

-   You start up the machine and set it to the right recipe, quantity, date, etc;
-   You ensure that the correct film is present in the machine;
-   You perform small-scale malfunction and/or maintenance activities to the machine and report any deviations;
-   You perform cleaning tasks on the machine;
-   You instruct and guide colleagues who work on the production line and you answer their questions;
-   You also work on the production line and set the right example. 

It goes without saying that quality and safety are of paramount importance to you. You follow the regulations concerning quality assurance (HACCP) and carry out checks on this. You are a real team player! 

Working hours:

from 05:45 am until production is complete 

As of week 16-2022 (start high season)

-  05:45 am – 14:30 pm
-  14:00 – 23:00 pm

You are available on approximately 25 Saturdays a year (twice a month)

- Have work experience in a similar position; 
- Have sufficient technical insight to solve small breakdowns;
- Feel good in a dynamic and sometimes hectic environment;
- You know how to get to work and enjoy being physically active;
- Can stand the cold (4 to 6 degrees);
- Like to work fulltime in shifts (early and late or extended shifts) and is willing to work on Saturdays once every fortnight;
- Have natural superiority, shows decisiveness, is result-oriented and flexible;
- Have a good command of the Dutch or English or Polisch language.
- You live in the Helmond/Eindhoven or Venray/Venlo area

Are You Our New Kitchen Steward?Are you hardworking, detail-oriented and proud of creating a clean and organised workplace? Then you could be the Kitchen Steward we are looking for at Hilton Garden Inn Leiden. We are looking for a part-time Steward for 24 hours a week! As a Kitchen Steward, you ensure that all dishes, kitchen utensils and equipment used by our Food & Beverage operation are cleaned thoroughly and ready for use. You work early and/or late shifts in the kitchen and stewarding area and collaborate closely with the Kitchen and Food & Beverage teams.What will you be doing?&middot;        Working with the team to create an excellent guest experience&middot;        Cleaning and correctly storing dishes, kitchen utensils and equipment&middot;        Keeping the stewarding area clean, safe and organised&middot;        Polishing and sorting cutlery, glassware and crockery&middot;        Using cleaning materials and equipment safely and responsibly&middot;        Following hygiene, food safety and health and safety standards&middot;        Supporting the Kitchen and Food & Beverage teams whenever needed

Functie-eisen:
Who are we looking for?&middot;        You are a reliable team player with a positive attitude&middot;        You are punctual and have a keen eye for detail&middot;        You enjoy working in a clean, organised environment&middot;        You are flexible and available for different shifts, including weekends and public holidays&middot;        You have a basic command of Dutch and/or English&middot;        Previous experience in a kitchen or stewarding role is welcome, but not essentialWhat do we offer?&middot;        A welcoming workplace within a diverse and international team&middot;        A dynamic hotel environment where teamwork and initiative are valued&middot;        Regular internal and external training and opportunities to grow within the hotel and Hilton&middot;        Access to Hilton's learning and development programmes&middot;

Are you someone who enjoys physical work and are you looking for a full-time position in day shift? Then we have a great opportunity for you! For Dorel Juvenile in Helmond, we are looking for a motivated Loader & Unloader who is ready to roll up their sleeves.Together with your colleagues, you will ensure that goods are processed correctly and efficiently. You will stay active throughout the day and play an important role in the logistics process.

What will you do?

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Checking and processing incoming goods;
- Packing and preparing outgoing shipments for dispatch;
- Storing products in the correct warehouse locations;
- Assisting with stock counts and inventory management;
- Maintaining a neat, safe, and organized working environment.

- You speak Dutch or English;
- You are physically fit and enjoy active work;
- You can travel independently to Helmond;
- You are available for day shifts from 08:00 AM to 04:30 PM;
- Experience in logistics is a plus, but not required.

SamenvattingStart as an Order Picker in Nieuwegein and make sure Albert Heijn supermarkets receive their products on time. Earn €14.99 gross per hour and allowances for working in shifts. Stay active throughout your working day, work with a friendly team, and make a difference every day. Good work!Over de functieAs an Orderpicker at this logistics organization in Nieuwegein, you make sure supermarkets receive their fresh products every day. Using a modern voice-picking system, available in Dutch, English, Polish, and Ukrainian, you collect orders in the warehouse. You walk a lot, pick products from shelves, and prepare orders for transport. You work quickly and accurately, because the stores depend on you. The job takes place in a refrigerated environment (around 4°C), so it’s important you are comfortable with cooler temperatures. You’ll receive clear instructions through the voice-picking system so you know exactly which products to collect.
Your tasks:
- Collecting products using a voice-picking system;
- Preparing and organizing trolleys for shipment;
- Checking product quantities and quality.

This job is for 40 hours per week. Your shifts will be scheduled as follows:
- Morning shift: 05:00–14:30
- Night shift: 19:30–04:00

Over het bedrijfAt your new workplace in Nieuwegein, you’ll work alongside colleagues from different countries towards one shared goal: making sure supermarkets across the Netherlands receive their fresh products on time. The atmosphere is friendly and welcoming. Colleagues help each other when needed, chat during breaks, and always have time for a joke. Together, you contribute to something that people rely on every day.
Wat wij vragen- You have your own accomodation in The Netherlands. For this job we don't provide housing;
- You speak Dutch, English, or Polish;
- You’re physically fit and able to perform physical work;
- You’re comfortable working in a chilled environment (around 4°C);
- You’re flexible and willing to work week

As a Warehouse Employee at DHL in Weert, you’ll be responsible for various logistics activities within the warehouse. Your tasks may include receiving, checking, storing, picking, and preparing goods for shipment. You’ll also work with Material Handling Equipment (MHE), such as an EPT or stacker, after receiving the appropriate training.

You’ll make sure that products are processed accurately and efficiently and that the warehouse runs smoothly. Because you’ll be working with ASML-related products, precision, responsibility, and following procedures are very important.

- You are 18 years or older (due to working hours);
- You have previous work experience in logistics, warehousing, or a similar environment;
- You’re available full-time (40 hours per week), either in two shifts or during the day;
- You’re able to request a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You have a basic understanding of English, as it is used daily in the warehouse;
- You’re eager to learn new skills, such as operating an EPT or stacker;
- You are comfortable working in a structured and fast-paced logistics environment.
